<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Third Anglo-Afghan War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1919">1919</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Third Anglo-Afghan War was a brief conflict in May 1919, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">Emir</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amanullah-khan">Amanullah Khan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> sent troops across the frontier of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-india">British India</a>. The British, using aircraft and superior numbers, checked the advance, but a war-weary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> agreed to the Treaty of Rawalpindi in August 1919, which recognised Afghanistan's full independence in foreign affairs.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/third-anglo-afghan-war.jpg" alt="Third Anglo-Afghan War" width="320" height="407" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sergeant EW Macro · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Soldiers_in_action_at_Kohat_during_the_Third_Anglo-Afghan_War.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
